    { q: 'NEA-style task: Plan an experiment to find the concentration of cornflour that produces a coating sauce. State the variables. [6]', m: 6, ms: ['independent variable: mass/percentage of cornflour (e.g. 2, 4, 6, 8%)', 'dependent variable: viscosity measured by line spread test / flow time', 'control variables: volume and type of milk, heating temperature/time, stirring, temperature at testing, pan', 'method: blend, heat to boiling while stirring, simmer 2 min, test at set temperature', 'repeat for reliability / calculate mean', 'success criterion defined (e.g. line spread 3–5 cm = coating)'] },
    { q: 'Explain how sugar crystallisation can be controlled to make smooth fudge. [4]', m: 4, ms: ['sugar syrup boiled to soft-ball stage 112–116 °C', 'avoid stirring during boiling / wash crystals from pan sides', 'cool slightly, then beat to form many small crystals', 'interfering agents (butter, milk/cream, glucose) prevent large crystals'] }
