    { h: 'Matching the audience', html: `
<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Audience</th><th>What they want</th><th>Suitable methods</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>Academic</b> (teachers, professors, peers)</td><td>full method, data, statistics, references, limitations — can the study be repeated?</td><td>research report (abstract, introduction, method, results, discussion, conclusion, references); academic presentation or poster</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Industry professionals</b> (food scientists, chefs, product developers, food safety inspectors)</td><td>practical implications — cost, processing, shelf life, safety, recommendations</td><td>technical report, presentation with data slides, product specification, executive summary</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Consumers</b> (public, customers, bloggers, journalists)</td><td>simple, engaging, relevant messages — “what does it mean for me?”</td><td><b>infographics</b>, <b>blogs</b>, <b>news articles</b>, social media posts, short videos</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Government and regulators</b> (food standards agencies, public health officials, policy makers)</td><td>evidence-based, concise, population impact, policy options</td><td>policy brief / report with key findings and recommendations; presentation</td></tr></table></div>` },
    { h: 'Presentation methods', html: `
<ul><li><b>Infographics</b> — visual summaries: icons, a few key statistics, clear charts; ideal for consumers and quick briefings; risk of oversimplifying.</li>
<li><b>Research reports</b> — detailed, structured, referenced; ideal for academic and technical readers; long.</li>
<li><b>Presentations</b> — slides plus speaking; tailor detail to audience; allow questions.</li>
<li><b>News articles</b> — headline, key finding first, quotes, plain language; wide reach.</li>
<li><b>Blogs</b> — informal, personal, interactive; good for consumer engagement; lower credibility unless referenced.</li></ul>
<div class="box tip"><b class="lbl">Good practice</b><p>Lead with the key finding; use the right chart; label axes and units; avoid jargon for lay audiences; state limitations honestly; cite sources.</p></div>` }
